\begin_layout Title
What the Paper Leaves Out: Reconstructing the Full Wang & Haiting Simulation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Author
Bampaliaris Nikolaos
\end_layout

\begin_layout Date
15-10-2026
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Summary
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Wang & Haiting paper describes the 
\series bold
framework
\series default
 of its space-charge model: the charge density, the cone-shaped charge region, the field components and the drift equation. It does 
\series bold
not
\series default
 give everything needed to run the simulation again. Some of the missing pieces only affect the detail of Figures 3 to 5; others are the core of Figures 6 to 8 (inception voltage, streamer length and charge against the front time of the impulse). There, the paper says that the models were “established” in an earlier paper written in Chinese (reference [9] of the paper) and gives no equations.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A complete simulation therefore has to be 
\series bold
reconstructed
\series default
: each missing piece is filled with a standard model from the literature of long air-gap discharges, every choice is documented, and the result is judged by how well it reproduces the 
\series bold
trends and magnitudes
\series default
 of the paper's figures rather than by an exact match. This note lists what the paper provides, what we have reconstructed so far for Figures 3 to 5, and what is still missing for Figures 6 to 8, with the candidate model for each gap.
\end_layout

