consistency
\series default
 with Figures 3 to 5 when the same rules are applied to that case.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Each assumption should be accompanied by a sensitivity check, so that the thesis can show which conclusions depend on it and which do not.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Conclusion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The paper is a summary of a larger model. It gives enough to understand the physics and to reproduce the field calculations of Figures 3 to 5 approximately, but not enough to reproduce Figures 6 to 8 directly. Reproducing the full simulation requires reconstructing the inception, streamer-length and second-streamer rules from the standard literature on long air gaps.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Suggested wording for the thesis:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
The original paper describes the space-charge model and its results but omits several elements needed to reproduce them, notably the applied-field model, the condition that fixes the cone angle, and the inception and streamer-length criteria behind its parametric results, which are published only in an earlier Chinese-language paper. These elements were reconstructed from established models of long air-gap discharges, each assumption is stated explicitly, and the reconstruction is validated against the trends and magnitudes of the published results.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Reproducibility
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This note summarizes notes 01 (Figure 3), 02 (Figure 4) and 03 (Figure 5) and the scripts behind them: wh_fig3_reproduction.py, wh_fig4_reproduction.py, wh_fig5_reproduction.py and compare_datasets.py. The statements about the paper refer to the copy in Theory/Resources/. No new calculation was made for this note.
